WEBVTT

00:02:59.297 --> 00:03:00.963
But then we have unhealthy guilt

00:03:00.997 --> 00:03:05.530
where maybe the guilt that we're feeling
is adopted through values

00:03:05.563 --> 00:03:07.297
that we don't necessarily hold

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.863
or boundaries that we
don't necessarily want to hold.

00:03:09.897 --> 00:03:11.097
So long-term guilt --

00:03:11.097 --> 00:03:13.497
guilt is not necessarily
a negative emotion.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.597
It's really important to understand
that differentiation,

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.063
that guilt is something
that can really guide us.

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:21.597
And like any emotion,
it's telling us something

00:03:21.597 --> 00:03:24.797
and we must listen to it
before we decide how to handle it.

00:03:25.397 --> 00:03:26.563
CSB: Yeah.

00:03:26.563 --> 00:03:28.097
And in the unhealthy situation,

00:03:28.097 --> 00:03:30.663
what are some helpful strategies
for dealing with it?